What is the difference between Input and Output in Java I/O?
Input is something we can say that we can take it from client side and process it accordingly ,it can be of any form or data or files .
Output is something that server will return upon requesting or performing certain actions by client .

2. What is the difference between byte streams and character streams? Give one example use case for each.
Byte streams are used for input and output where the data is stored in form of binary values eg. photos and videos.
Character stream is used for input and output where the data is stored in the form of text values like json , xml etc.

3. What is the purpose of BufferedReader?
BufferReader is used when we have to read all the contents of file at once not byte by byte or character by character , it first reads the whole file at once .

